text.en:
Energy Projects of National Significance (EPS). EPS are
major energy projects for power generation, transmission and/or ancillary services
including those required to maintain grid stability and security, identified and
endorsed by the DOE as "projects of national significance" that are in consonance
with the policy thrusts and specific goals of the PEP, and which possess any of the
following attributes:
significant capital investment of at least P3.5 Billion:
significant contribution to the country's economic development;
significant consequential economic impact;
significant potential contribution to the country's balance of payments;
significant impact on the environment;
complex technical processes and engineering designs; and/or
significant infrastructure requirements.
